    <div class="alpheios-lex-entry" lemma-id="n35284" body-key=""><b><span class="alpheios-lex-la" lang="lat">per-nĭmĭus</span></b> , a,
		um, adj., <div class="alpheios-lex-lex_sense alpheios-lex-lex_sense1"><b>I.</b><i>quite too great</i>, <i>altogether too
				much</i>: 
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-la" lang="lat">nimium inter vos ac pernimium interest,</span>”
				 <i><span class="en">Ter.
					Ad. 3, 3, 39</span></i>
			; 
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-la" lang="lat">in tmesi: per parce nimium,</span>”
				 <i><span class="en">id.
					And. 2, 6, 24</span></i>
			.—<i>Adv.</i>: <b><span class="alpheios-lex-la" lang="lat">pernĭmĭum</span></b> , <i>altogether too much</i>: 
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-la" lang="lat">interpretatio pernimium severa,</span>”
				<i>altogether too severe</i>,
				 <i><span class="en">Dig.
					48, 3, 2</span></i>
			.</div>
